;; tags: control-flow, loops, backward-branch
;; expect: 45
;; Iterative loop -- the canonical backward-branch pattern. `dotimes`
;; emits: init counter, label L, body, increment, cmp counter limit,
;; b.lt L. The `b.lt` is the backward edge; its offset is *negative*
;; and known at the moment of emission (no patching needed for this
;; direction, but the encoder must sign-extend correctly into the
;; imm19 field of the conditional-branch encoding). Sum 0+1+...+9 = 45.
(defun main ()
  (let ((sum 0))
    (dotimes (i 10)
      (set! sum (+ sum i)))
    (format #t "~D~%" sum)))
